{"id": "EUVD-2026-108135", "enisaUuid": "510634d3-0f50-30a7-91c2-7a9d19e1abf1", "description": "Lotus through 0.10.2 contains an improper authentication vulnerability in the Go event ingestion middleware that validates API keys by prefix only, without checking the secret against the stored hashed_key. Attackers who know or obtain an API key prefix can submit usage events to POST /api/track/ as that organization, altering its metered usage and billing.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T10:57:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T10:57:49", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@leediay/BkUc3WL2Mx", "https://github.com/uselotus/lotus/blob/0.10.2/go/event-ingestion/authn/authn.go#L85-L95", "https://github.com/uselotus/lotus", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/lotus-through-0.10.2-improper-authentication-via-event-ingestion-api-key-prefix"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-115333", "GHSA-pcv2-4g25-r7qr"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "30cd25b4-eb3a-39c3-bd45-bebd1a6ec414", "product": {"name": "lotus", "vendor": {"name": "filecoin-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.10.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6e319cd3-c802-3137-b36f-fc7c8f28802d", "vendor": {"name": "uselotus"}}], "isExploited": false}